   \& Hlth; Int Council Res \& Innovat Bldg \& Construct; European Commiss
   Asia Pro Eco Programme Promot Sustainable Solut Environm Europe \& Asia;
   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {This paper presents a draft perception study of Displacement Ventilation
   (DV) system in a Field Environmental Chamber (FEC) with tropically
   acclimatized subjects. A total of 60 subjects, 30 males and 30 females,
   were exposed to 3 vertical air temperature gradients, 1, 3 \& 5 K/m.
   between 0.1 and 1.1 m heights and 3 room air temperatures, 20, 23 \& 26
   degrees C at 0.6 m height for a 3-hour period. Air velocity near the
   subjects was maintained at below 0.2 m/s. Relative Humidity (RH) at 0.6
   m height and fresh air provision was fixed at 50\% and 10 l/s/p
   respectively. It was found that in the space served by DV system, draft
   perception was insignificantly affected by temperature gradient. Room
   air temperature had greater impact on percentage dissatisfied due to air
   movement than temperature gradient. Cold sensation would add draft risk
   and warm sensation would increase percentage dissatisfied due to
   insufficient air movement.},
