   Technology (REIT 2010), Int Soc Resource Environm Informat Technol,
   Kaifeng, PEOPLES R CHINA, AUG 19-21, 2010},
Organization = {Int Soc Resource Environm Informat Technol},
Abstract = {With attempts to improve the photocatalytic activity of titanium dioxide
   (TiO2) catalysts and also extend the light absorption towards the
   visible light region, a novel lanthanum and iodine co-doped TiO2
   photocatalyst (La/I/TiO2) was synthesized by sol-gel method, and
   characterized by X-ray diffraction and transmission electron microscopy.
   Activities of prepared photocatalysts were evaluated by decomposing
   methyl orange solution as model compound to photocatalytic degradation.
   Compared with the pure TiO2 and La doped TiO2 catalysts, the ternary
   compound La/I/TiO2 photocatalyst (the molar percent of La is 3.2\%)
   calcined at 450 degrees C for 2h showed the strongest absorption for
   visible light and highest activities for degradation of methyl orange
   under irradiation of visible light. It was also discovered that the
   doping of La reduced slightly the phase transformation temperature of
   TiO2 from anatase to rutile, suppress the growth of TiO2 grains and
   raise the specific surface area.},
