Abstract = {The current paper presents the outputs of the study on the feasibility
   of rainwater use for high-rise residential envelopes for four Australian
   cities, Melbourne, Sydney, Perth and Darwin. Various climate data,
   raintank dimension changing and different levels of water demand
   management techniques have been explored, which are discussed in views
   of tank water use, percentage of drinking water substitution. In terms
   of the impact of tank size and water demand measures, the latter
   outperforms than the former. The results of this analysis demonstrate
   that Sydney is more suited to rainwater use, followed by Melbourne,
   Perth and Darwin. This study endeavors to provide a paradigm of
   rainwater use for water authorities and urban designers of Australian
   cities.},
