Abstract = {Organosepiolite has been prepared by exchanging with
   hexadecyltrimethylammonium bromide (CTAB) as a modifier. The adsorption
   kinetics and thermodynamics of methyl orange from aqueous solutions onto
   organosepiolite are studied, then the adsorption principle is discussed.
   The results of XRD and FTIR show that sepiolite can be well modified by
   treating with CAB. The results indicate that the adsorption isotherm for
   methyl orange accords with the Langumir equation. The adsorption
   enthalpy and entropy changes are -13.54 kJ/mol and -32.8.1/(mol.K),
   respectively. And the adsorption exhibits spontaneous physical
   adsorption and exothermic. The adsorption dynamics follows the laws of
   pseudo-second-order kinetics with the energy of activation is
   6.36kJ/mol.},
