   and Prospects, Sibiu, ROMANIA, JUN 03-05, 2011},
Abstract = {Nonverbal sensitivity, as the ability to decode others' nonverbal
   behavior has been assessed using two international standardized tests
   PONS (Rosenthal et al., 1979), respectively DANVA (Nowicki \& Duke,
   1994). The results support the idea of individual's differences in
   access and use information on visual and audio channels, on static and
   dynamic items. Testing 146 college students we predict different
   abilities to decode face-only items, body-only items and paralanguage
   items in relation with their cognitive styles (TSI, Sternberg \& Wagner,
   1992). Additional information about the two tests comparative validity
   is presented.},
