   30-NOV 02, 2014},
Organization = {World Psychiat Assoc; Int Neuropsychiatr Assoc},
Abstract = {The ``dyn4{''} framework for anxio-affective ``appropriation wave
   disorders{''} mirrors the segregated and oscillating three CSTC-circuits
   that map to the psychological dimensions Thought-{''}T{''},
   Action-{''}A{''}, and Mood-{''}M{''}. The 8 corners of their cubic phase
   space are called NEED-tam, FEAR-tAm, JOY-tAM etc.. They connect
   reciprocally via 56 vectors expressing natural, and clinical, language
   terms: e.g. ``Cognizance-35{''} from F3-tAM to I5-TaM. By syllogisms
   (AXINN 1994) ``T{''} by using ``All{''} to ``not Some{''} graduates the
   ``either/or{''} of ``A{''}.
   The dyadic extension of ``dyn4{''} generates 64 relations. It allows to
   conceive cases and interventions in individual and family therapy.
   Roadblocks resolve by accepting all emotions and by evoking precise
   paths of resolution by language, which change the intensities in
   ``T{''}, ``A{''}, and/or ``M{''}.},
