   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {This paper studied the thermal performance of the shape-stabilized phase
   change material. The shape-stabilized phase change materials include
   paraffin mixtures and high-density polyethylene. The paraffin mixtures
   was made by mixing liquid paraffin with 46\# paraffin, 48\# paraffin or
   n-Octadecane and mixing n-Heptadecane with 48\# paraffin. The phase
   change temperatures of these mixtures are between 21 and 28 degrees C
   and they have higher phase change latent heats. They are suitable to use
   in the wall. The shape-stabilized phase change materials were made by
   mixing paraffin mixtures with high-density polyethylene respectively in
   different proportion. The phase change temperatures, the phase change
   latent heats, the uniformity and stability of the shape-stabilized phase
   change materials were studied experimentally by DSC. The research shows
   that the prepared shape-stabilized phase change materials are the ideal
   energy storage materials used in the wall.},
