Note = {6th International Conference on Applied Human Factors and Ergonomics
   (AHFE), Las Vegas, NV, JUL 26-30, 2015},
Abstract = {When interacting with a robot, the level of mental workload, comfort and
   trust during the interaction are decisive factors for an effective
   interaction. Hence, current research focuses on the concept, whether
   ascribing gantry robot in assembly with anthropomorphic movements can
   lead to a better anticipation of its behavior by the human operator.
   Therefore, in an empirical study the effect of different degrees of
   anthropomorphism should be compared. This is based on the scientific
   research concerning the neural activity of the human brain when watching
   someone performing an action. Within the study videos of a virtual
   gantry robot and a digital human model during placing movements were
   designed to use in the functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI). The
   aim is to investigate the underlying brain mechanism during observing
   the movements of the two models. (C) 2015 The Authors. Published by
   Elsevier B.V.},
