Note = {2nd World Conference on Psychology, Counselling and Guidance (WCPCG),
   Antalya, TURKEY, MAY 25-29, 2011},
Abstract = {Alexithymia and self-regulation of patients with substance abuse
   disorder and normal individuals were compared in an Iranian population.
   360 volunteers (180 patients, 180 normals) completed the Toronto
   Alexithymia Scale (TAS-20) and the Self-Regulation Inventory (SRI-25).
   Patients with substance abuse disorder scored significantly higher than
   normal individuals on alexithymia and the non-clinical sample had higher
   rates of self-regulation than clinical sample. The relation between
   alexithymia and substance abuse can be explained in terms of several
   mechanisms including distance from negative emotions, self-medication,
   facilitating verbal and emotional communications. Self-regulation
   dysfunction is supposed to be related to substance abuse disorder
   through deficit of self-control and affect regulation. (C) 2011
