Note = {Symposium on Future Landscapes and the Future of Landscape Ecology at
   the World Congress of the
   International-Association-for-Landscape-Ecology (IALE 95), TOULOUSE,
   FRANCE, AUG, 1995},
Organization = {Int Assoc Landscape Ecol},
Abstract = {This paper summarizes the geographic information system (GIS) and
   modelling activities of the Munich Research Association for Agricultural
   Ecosystems (FAM), which is a joint project of the GSF-National Research
   Centre for Environment and Health, Oberschleissheim, and the Technical
   University of Munich. In particular, the agro-ecological information
   system (AIS) within the FAM will be presented. Simulation models will be
   provided in a GIS to forecast and assess ecological risks of different
   management practices. The AIS is based on two different scales: one is a
   farm called `Klostergut Scheyern' (149 ha), designed as a monitoring
   network with a cell resolution of 50m x 50m, the other is the
   surrounding area, a landscape of 547 km(2). The paper describes the
   spatial input data as well as the model structure of the two different
   scales. Finally, first results for calculating the soil water budget on
   the farm level, and nitrate leaching on the landscape level will be
   presented.},
