   Assoc Sci \& Technol, China Ctr Int Sci \& Technol Exchange; OPCW},
Abstract = {The phospholipid fatty acids (PLFA) as biomarkers of microbial community
   structures were appointed to elaborate the mobilization of arsenic (As)
   in groundwater from Datong Basin. The results showed that saturated
   fatty acids 16:0, 18:0, monounsaturated fatty acids 16:1 omega 9, 18:1
   omega 9, and cyclopropane fatty acids 17:0, 19:0 had relatively high
   contents. This may imply the significant impact of dominant Des
   ulfbbacter and Clostridium on the mobilization of As in the shallow
   groundwater. Sulfate-reducing bacteria and Fe-reducing bacteria can
   mediate the reductive dissolution of As-bearing Fe oxides/hydroxides to
   cause the release of As into groundwater.},
