   PREVENTION, IMPACT, ABATEMENT, CHICAGO, IL, SEP 19-24, 1993},
Organization = {INT ASSOC WATER QUAL; USDA, WORKING GRP WATER QUAL; US DEPT TRANSPORT,
   FED HIGHWAY ADM; US EPA, REG 5; US EPA, ENVIRONM RES LAB, ATHENS
   MARQUETTE UNIV},
Abstract = {The province of Pavia, in Northern Italy, is an intensively cultivated
   agricultural area with substantial urban development. Groundwater
   supplies constitute almost all the potable water available to the
   resident population. Concern exists about the fate of herbicides applied
   to farm fields that have been found in measurable quantities in drinking
   water supplies. This paper describes at first the general environmental
   conditions and land use activity pattern in which the diffuse
   contamination occurs, history of contaminant detection is correlated to
   external interventions, such as government regulations, and the findings
   of the monitoring process are then illustrated. A mathematical model of
   groundwater transport is then illustrated and its predictions are
   compared with monitoring findings.},
