   AUSTRALIA, AUG 20-24, 2007},
Organization = {Hlth Informat Soc Australia},
Abstract = {The aim of this project is to contribute to limiting the risk of CHIS
   (computerised hospital information system) failure by identifying
   factors which are associated with the successful implementation of CHISs
   in district and regional hospitals in South Africa (SA). Case studies
   were conducted in four regional hospitals in the Western Cape province
   of SA to obtain data about user perceptions of the success or lack of
   success of the CHISs in use. A conceptual model of CHIS use has been
   developed based on the results of the case studies, in order to assist
   in the interpretation of the differing experiences across the hospitals.
   Key factors in the conceptual model are perception of usefulness of the
   CHIS and management commitment to ensuring CHIS success, which in turn
   are related to effective use of CHIS and for CHIS outputs, and
   allocation of resources for CHIS further development Further development
   of the model will be influenced by the next phase of this project: a
   survey of district and regional hospitals in two SA provinces.},
